   "id": null,
   "title": "Design & hull",
   "intro": "The new Solaris 44 has been conceived to reinterpret one of the brand’s most successful models, bringing it into line with the design language that defines the latest yachts in the range. A more open stern, shorter side decks with integrated steps, redesigned helm seats, and a revised deck layout enhance its elegance, comfort, and onboard liveability.\nBelow deck, the design evolves with effortless sophistication. Flowing, curved lines take center stage, creating interiors that feel more harmonious and inviting, while refined new design details give the living spaces a contemporary and more sophisticated character.",
   "items": [],
   "images": []
  },
  {
   "kind": "block",
   "id": null,
   "title": "Interiors",
   "intro": "The interiors, developed in collaboration with 3-Studio, are offered in a single, timelessly classic layout. The L-shaped galley is located to port, while the accommodation comprises three cabins and two bathrooms, both featuring separate shower stalls. The interior design reflects exceptional craftsmanship and meticulous attention to detail, with cabinetry elegantly incorporating the hull windows. A key innovation is the extensive use of leather inserts and refined leather detailing throughout the interior, adding warmth, sophistication, and a distinctly premium feel.",
   "items": [],
   "images": []
  }
 ],
